            "created_at": "2025-08-27T22:57:20.664755+00:00",
            "notes": "### Powers\nThe power you take this round depends on what kind of a team you're facing, and what you want your build to play more into. \n- [God Ray](item_4abb5cdb-f113-4f21-aa0a-e67d95a11fd0): Really good for extra long-range damage, even on snipers or flyers, as well as when you later get [Liquid Nitrogen](item_a8d99526-05a3-4405-babb-b025479b1b98) for applying the debuff for longer periods of time due to the burn. \nHowever, if they either have cleanses or are running a comp that's trying to get up close and in your face/diving you, this becomes less useful. \n- [Sk\u00f6ldkastning](item_a6c36dee-d961-428b-b27c-93ba5ef377d8): This ability is a little weird to get used to, but if you're able to hit multiple targets with it combined with an item we'll get later, [Scavenged Steel](item_fb9d2d13-db05-46fa-b3c6-07495b1872a4), you end up getting your ult insanely quickly. Plus, this can travel through shields, so if you're struggling to hit people through Rein/Sigma/Winston barriers and thus working with low inspire uptime, this ability will go through them and trigger it. \nHowever, you do have to give up your shield bash for it. If you're careful with timing it, you can save the use of it by not using melee/primary afterwards, but still. That, and if they don't have barriers you can't whipshot through then you're kinda missing out on damage through burning them. \n\nGenerally, I'd lean more towards [God Ray](item_4abb5cdb-f113-4f21-aa0a-e67d95a11fd0), but both powers can be a lot of fun. Whichever you don't pick now you'll *probably* get round 7 instead. (Not round 5, but there's a reason for that)\n\n### Items\nMost games you can just minmax high AP this round, (though it's a little awkward because we end up with less AP next round), but if you're facing enemies you want to slow or force less healing upon, then consider taking either [Liquid Nitrogen](item_a8d99526-05a3-4405-babb-b025479b1b98) or [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505).\n\nIf you got [Sk\u00f6ldkastning](item_a6c36dee-d961-428b-b27c-93ba5ef377d8) this round, you could also consider getting [Scavenged Steel](item_fb9d2d13-db05-46fa-b3c6-07495b1872a4) early, as each hit with your shield boomerang counts for 3% ult charge. If they're often grouped up, this could be great for you. Though, your rally isn't super buffed yet like it will be later, it's still nice to get quick ults. Keep in mind though, this item doesn't give you **any** ability power, so you'll end up with less healing output for this round because of it.\n\n### TO NOTE:\nIn case you aren't aware, [Kiriko](hero_70a0ac5c-2a55-4fab-beeb-2f570886426f)'s Suzu cleanses negative effects like burning, or speed/healing debuffs like from [Liquid Nitrogen](item_a8d99526-05a3-4405-babb-b025479b1b98)/[Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505). Normally, this might just make her use her ability, which is good, but if she has [Cleansing Charge](item_4721f307-30d2-4fc1-a10b-6de7141deb68), this can just give her ult faster, especially when paired with CDR and [Two-Zu](item_80f16d3e-a4c0-4fa8-90b1-a0f033a1a77b). Something to keep in mind if she's on the enemy team.",
